<title>UK: Austria trade seeks free mkt barley at EU tender.</title>
<headline>Austria trade seeks free mkt barley at EU tender.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian traders have submitted bids for 8,000 tonnes of free market barley at Thursday's EU grains tender, member state officials said.</p>
<p>The bids are for a refund ranging from 23.90 to 26.98 Ecus per tonne, the officials said. There were no bids for other grains.</p>
<p>The EU cereals management committee will adjudicate tender bids at its meeting on Thursday afternoon. --Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
